    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d375">

                <pb facs="0570" n="460" xml:id="pg460"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5344: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation to the Sixth
                        International Conference of American States</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hughes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-02-01T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 1,
                                1928—8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 1—7:45
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>60. From White. I have been assured by Cuadra Pasos that he and Zepeda are
                    cabling influential members of the Conservative Party to support the electoral
                    law when the subject is discussed by the Council of Notables of the Conservative
                    Party when it meets Sunday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
